  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/8d87383a-d7c1-4c29-b9bc-af226b416c73-image.png\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 141px;\" /></p><p>Acceleration of a particle in uniform circular motion&nbsp;is directed towards the centre of the circle and its magnitude is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>R</mi></mfrac></math>. The radius vector is<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mover accent=\"true\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mover accent=\"true\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p>Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mover accent=\"true\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mover accent=\"true\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></math></p>",
